(Description)
There is an integer array nums sorted in ascending order (with distinct values).

Prior to being passed to your function, nums is possibly left rotated at an unknown index k (1 <= k < nums.length) such that 
the resulting array is [nums[k], nums[k+1], ..., nums[n-1], nums[0], nums[1], ..., nums[k-1]] (0-indexed). 
For example, [0,1,2,4,5,6,7] might be left rotated by 3 indices and become [4,5,6,7,0,1,2].

Given the array nums after the possible rotation and an integer target, return the index of target if it is in nums, or -1 if it is not in nums.

You must write an algorithm with O(log n) runtime complexity.

--- Solution ---
class Solution {
    public int search(int[] nums, int target) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = nums.length - 1;

        while (left <= right) {
            int med = (int) Math.floor((left + right)/2);

            if (nums[med] == target) {
                return med;
            }
            
            if (nums[left] <= nums[med]) {
                if (nums[left] <= target && target < nums[med]) {
                    right = med - 1;
                }
                else {
                    left = med + 1;
                }
            }
            else {
                if (nums[med] < target && target <= nums[right]) {
                    left = med + 1;
                }
                else {
                    right = med - 1;
                }
            }
        }

        return -1;
    }
}

--- Approach ---
Because of the limited time complexity, O(log n), it was not possible to use loop statement to check all of the integers in the array.
However, the array was sorted even though it was rotated, integers could be searched followed by a rule.

[Search Algorithm]
There are two points, left & right.
Each step it finds the med point of left and right and pivot the med integer.
At this level, there are two cases.
1. left number is less or equal than pivoted number => Means that left part was sorted well.
2. else case : left number is bigger than pivoted number => Means that left part was rotated, But it gurantees that right part was sorted at least.

Then, each cases check the target number is involved in the sorted parts or not & moving the left and right pointer followed by the result.
